# @APP_NAME@

PySide6 operations monitor with a responsive shell, KPI cards, live
`LineChart`, filterable `DataGrid`, native FluentQt components, and explicit
domain, application, infrastructure, and UI boundaries.

```bash
python -m venv .venv
python -m pip install -e .
python -m unittest discover -s tests
@APP_ID@
```

The app package composes dependencies. Domain and application modules remain
independent of Qt, infrastructure owns telemetry sources, and UI modules only
render application state and publish user intent.

`ui/components/workbench_shell.py` owns wide/narrow shell geometry. Adapt
`ui/pages/monitor_page.py` and `infrastructure/local_telemetry_repository.py`
for your own device metrics, serial streams, or service endpoints.

## Quality report

After the window starts cleanly, emit the same native Inspector report as the
C++ starter:

```bash
@APP_ID@ --quality-report
```

The command prints versioned JSON and exits. It does not change the interface.
